       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose, not whether someone approved it. A 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine is a recognized overdose level. It could seriously harm the patient. The order also hasn't been confirmed by a prescriber who has assessed the patient and can take clinical responsibility for it.\n\nHere are the ways forward:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose.** If you or the treating team meant a normal dose, I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away. Just tell me which.\n- **Have the prescriber place or confirm the order.** The treating physician can enter it directly or contact me. If they believe 50 mg is necessary, they should document why. Pharmacy should review it before anything is dispensed.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** If you're unsure about the intended dose, the on-call pharmacist can quickly clarify with the care team.\n\nIf the patient's blood pressure is a concern right now, the care team should be told so they can assess the patient and choose appropriate treatment."
